# Jira comment edit backup

Jira cannot revert a comment overwrite.

Before any `addOrEditJiraIssueComment` (or equivalent) **with** `commentId`:

1. Fetch that comment as HTML (`responseContentFormat: html`).
2. Run `python3 ~/.agents/skills/plan-task-evidence/scripts/backup-jira-comment.py --issue <KEY> --comment-id <ID> --body-file <html>`.
3. Edit only if the script exits 0. Report the backup path in chat, never in the Jira body.

New comments (no `commentId`) skip this. Do not skip the backup because the comment is same-day, a re-run, or a plan said to edit in place.
